  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "Jks8hqbmUP3PexQVzYuxrQqe75U=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The Powerhouse CLI (`ph-cmd`) is the primary tool for managing Powerhouse projects. Key commands:\n\n- `ph init` - Initialize a new project (scaffolds directory structure from boilerplate)\n- `ph vetra --watch` - Launch Vetra Studio with live code generation (recommended)\n- `ph vetra --interactive` - Launch with confirmation prompts before generation\n- `ph connect` - Run Connect locally. It is a subcommand group over `studio`, `build`, `preview`, and `config`, defaulting to `studio`; `ph connect build` is the mandatory production build step\n- `ph generate` - Generate code. This is a **subcommand group**, not a flag-driven command; its subcommands are `all`, `document-model`, `editor`, `app`, `processor`, `subgraph`, `migration-file`\n  - `ph generate document-model --document <file>` - Generate code from an exported specification\n  - `ph generate editor --name <str> --document-type <str>` - Generate an editor template (the option is singular: `--document-type`)\n  - `ph generate app --name <str> --document-types <value>` - Generate a drive app; this replaced the old `--drive-editor`\n  - `ph generate subgraph --name <str>` and `ph generate processor --name <str> --type <str> --document-types <str>`\n- `ph reactor` / `ph switchboard` - Start the API service (`reactor` is an alias of `switchboard`)\n- `ph install <package>` / `ph uninstall <package>` - Manage published Powerhouse packages\n- `ph publish` - Publish the project to a registry\n- `ph login` - Create/link a Renown identity; `ph access-token` - mint a bearer token from that identity\n- `ph list` - List installed Powerhouse packages; `ph inspect <package>` - show a package's structure and config\n- `ph migrate` - Run migrations to a newer Powerhouse version\n- `ph use <tag>` - Switch dependency release tag; `ph use-local <path>` - point dependencies at a local monorepo checkout\n- `ph update` - Update dependencies to latest versions\n\nThe CLI supports four release tags: `latest` (stable), `staging`, `dev`, and `rc`. There is no `prod` tag, and `local` is not a tag either -- local monorepo dependencies are handled by the separate `ph use-local` command.\n\n_Corrected 2026-08-13 against Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:34.000Z"
    }
  },
